  willing to die for him joe mentions that  the citadel will rise from the ashes and  become a prosperous clan saying this  much he releases some water but only for  a few seconds after joe shuts off the  water supply the people go crazy and  fight for it joe warns the crowd to not  get too addicted with water so that they  will not resent its absence joe then  sends his lieutenant imperitor furiosa  who has a prosthetic arm to collect fuel  and bullets shortly after she leaves in  a war rig while several war boys  accompany her in smaller vehicles later  on the way furiosa diverts her rig and  starts heading east her war boys are  confused by the sudden change of plans  but since they are loyal to her they  don't ask much elsewhere joe finds out  about furious's change of direction and  immediately heads to his chambers where  he has locked his wives when he reaches  there he is stunned to find that they  are all gone a message on the wall reads  that their children will not be warlords  implying that they will have run away  from him here we get to know that  furiosa has betrayed her master and is  escaping the place with the women in the  next scene we are introduced to the  protagonist max a road warrior who is  searching for a righteous cause nowadays  he is constantly bothered by visions of  the dead who he couldn't protect from  the war as he is gazing around the  deserted place the war boys appear out  of nowhere prompting max to drive off  however he doesn't get far as the war  boys destroy his vehicle and tie him up  then they drag him to the citadel inside  the cave the warboys trim his hair and  beard they also make tattoos on his back  one being written as a universal donor  oh negative as they intend to use him as  a blood bank when they try to brand max  with a burning iron having the shape of  a skull he manages to free himself and  escape he fights several scavengers  along the way but just then he starts  getting visions of the dead this  distracts him momentarily allowing the  war boys to capture him again in the  next scene joe orders his war boys to go  i keep saying that word to go after  furiosa while everyone is preparing for  war an almost dead war boy named nux  takes max along with him as he  desperately needs blood he chains max to  his vehicle and transfuses his blood so  that he gets the constant energy  required for the battle following this  the whole gang drives off and uh is no  one gonna talk about that guitarist with  the flamethrower guitar okay meanwhile  furios's war rig is attacked by another  scavenging tribe buzzards she manages to  defeat them but soon notices the large  horde of soldiers sent by joe scared she  drives into a massive sandstorm in hopes  that she can lose her pursuers the plan  works  partially all of joe's minions stop  except for knox he is hell-bent on  pleasing his master having a lovely day  so he pours fuel into his car and  attempts to ram it with furious's war  rig his plan is to sacrifice his life  and to become a martyr while also  killing furiosa however due to the  sandstorm he loses control of the car  and crashes it nearby after a while max  rises from the sand and notices that he  is chained to knox who is still  unconscious on walking a bit further he  finds furiosa's rig where the five girls  are cleaning themselves up here we get  to know that one of the girls splendid  is nine months pregnant with joe's child  max asks the girls to cut off his chain  that ties him to knox but they fail to  do so just then furiosa notices joe's  men approaching in the distance she  prepares to leave with the girls but max  demands to be freed first with this the  two get into a fight max eventually  overpowers furiosa and even manages to  cut his chain off he then gets into the  war rig and drives away leaving everyone  behind what a prick as the girls think  that they're doomed the rig stops nearby  it turns out that furiosa has installed  a kill switch in the rig which only she  knows how to restart because of this max  reluctantly lets all the girls inside he  also promises to lead them to a place  called green place which is supposedly a  safe haven for girls but still has a  stupid-ass name later furiosa drives the  rig to a canyon ruled by biker bandits  called the rock riders she has already  made a deal with them which states that  they will get to pass the area in  exchange for 3 000 gallons of fuel as  furiosa gets out of the rig to negotiate  the rock riders spot the large horde of  joe's troops arriving this violates the  deal as furiosa mentioned that only a  few people would be passing through not  an entire city the bikers are furious  but before they can take any action  furiosa enters the rig and drives away  however the bikers are not going to let  up so easily on her so they start  following the rig with this an intense  chase ensues but once again the heroes  managed to kill the bad guys one by one  by this time the war boys have also  closed in on the rig as joe tries to  shoot at the reg splendid opens the door  and makes herself a shield for everyone  she is sure that joe will not hurt their  baby surprisingly he holds back as he is  adamant on giving birth to a successor  nux tries to console him that they will  get the girls back but this only angers  joe and he leaves nux behind meanwhile  as splendid tries to climb back inside  the rig she slips and falls joe tries to  save her but only ends up running her  over when he stops he finds splendid's  lifeless body and screams in anguish in  the next scene nux who is disappointed  with joe manages to enter the rig there  he changes sides and promises to help  the girls escape at first they are  skeptical about his motives but when nux  mentions that he doesn't have many days  left to live they take him in as they  drive through the night their rig  suddenly gets stuck in the mud to make  matters worse the bullet farmer gang  starts approaching them it turns